WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.040
- Well being from New York,
did you ever audition for SNL?

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:05.250
Cause you're hilarious.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.083
- I did.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:10.510
Back in the day, I think it was 1996,

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.090
I went to the Montreal Comedy Festival

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:15.610
which was really big for
comedians at the time.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:17.470
And I remember I had a little heat on me

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.330
and people were looking to sign me to

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.960
like a development deal.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.340
And then in the middle of that in Montreal

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.260
they called and said that
SNL wanted to see you.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.070
And I'd been a huge fan of
SNL growing up, my whole life.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.600
So they said, "Would you
come out and perform?"

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:31.550
And I said, "Sure, no problem,

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:32.570
I'd love to audition."

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.231
So I go there to audition
and right before I go on

00:00:35.231 --> 00:00:37.890
they say, "What kind of
characters do you have?"

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.200
And I was like, "I don't have characters,

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.330
I'm a stand up."

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:41.330
And they're like, "Oh okay,

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.200
I guess do your stand up."

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.850
And I didn't have any characters,

00:00:46.548 --> 00:00:48.430
and I stood in a room with a microphone,

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:51.030
no one there, it was pitch black.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.663
I did my whole act, not one laugh.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.440
I didn't hear anybody breathing in there.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:57.273
- Oh!

00:00:57.273 --> 00:00:59.270
- And I bombed so bad, I was the worst.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.615
It was the worst experience ever.

00:01:01.615 --> 00:01:02.652
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:02.652 --> 00:01:03.630
- And obviously I didn't get it.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:06.990
I didn't get it, but I
got a development deal.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:08.130
Because I didn't get it,

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.390
I was able to do The King of Queens,

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.820
so it actually worked out.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:12.840
- That's such a great story

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.470
for like up and coming comedians as well.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:15.530
Or like people just really wanting to

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:16.363
achieve their dream.

00:01:16.363 --> 00:01:19.650
It's like, I mean, myself included,

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.850
they're not all open doors.

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:22.907
Like, you know?

00:01:22.907 --> 00:01:23.740
- Right.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.200
- So yeah, you've gotta be
able to like handle that

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.250
and build that character.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:30.340
But I think that's amazing,
cause you're so funny.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.370
Well, they missed out, is
what I'm saying, Kevin.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.203
- That's right.

00:01:34.203 --> 00:01:35.320
I appreciate that, Kelly.

